{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And the taskmasters pressed.</b> A verb in the active voice (פועל יוצא), like the word שב and like the word מש; it is found sometimes as a transitive verb and sometimes as intransitive." "And the sense of לאמר: saying to them." "<b>Day by day.</b> Like \"from new moon to new moon\" (Isaiah 66:23)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Resolved פועל יוצא as active/transitive voice and עומד as intransitive, following standard medieval Hebrew grammatical terminology."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:56.441492232Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}